<title>CANADA: CRICKET-INDIA 173-2 BEAT PAKISTAN 170-9.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-INDIA 173-2 BEAT PAKISTAN 170-9.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>India defeated Pakistan by eight wickets in the first match of the Sahara Cup cricket series at the Toronto Cricket, Skating and Curling ground here on Monday.</p>
<p>Pakistan compiled 170-9 off their maximum 33 overs in the rain-affected match, while India replied with 173-2 off 29.5 overs.</p>
<p>Scores:</p>
<p>India 173-2 (Sachin Tendulkar 89no, Rahul Dravid 39)</p>
<p>Pakistan 170-9 (Saeed Anwar 46; Javagal Srinath three for 23, Anil Kumble three for 32)</p>
